@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Deploy Planner
  "Diffs a site's local build folder against its server path using rsync dry-run and returns plan counts."

  Provides:
    - deploy.Runner @source("symbol:Runner")
    - deploy.Planner @source("symbol:Planner")
    - deploy.NewPlanner @source("symbol:NewPlanner")
    - deploy.Plan @source("symbol:Plan")
    - deploy.PlanOptions @source("symbol:PlanOptions")
    - deploy.Planner.Plan
    - deploy.ParseCompareOutput @source("symbol:ParseCompareOutput")
    - deploy.DefaultFilters @source("symbol:DefaultFilters")

  Consumes:
    - config.Site
    - remote.CompareDryRunRequest
    - remote.RsyncDestination
    - remote.SSHOptionsFromServer

  Invariants:
    - Plan MUST require the site's build folder, path, and server, failing with a hint to set build: when the folder is unset
    - Plan MUST run rsync with dry-run, itemize-changes, and stats only — no bytes transferred
    - Plan MUST apply DefaultFilters so dotfiles and dot-directories at any depth are never planned for transfer, except /.well-known/ at the build root
    - Excluded remote paths MUST be protected from --delete (no --delete-excluded)
    - ParseCompareOutput MUST derive new, changed, unchanged, remove, and bytes-to-send from rsync stats
    - ParseCompareOutput MUST count regular files only (never directories) and MUST accept thousands separators and a trailing kind breakdown such as "(reg: 1,205, dir: 2)"

  OutOfScope:
    - Running deploy transfers (future M-061)
    - CLI commands for deploy and status (future M-061)
    - Share object store or manifest interaction

  Scenario (happy-path): Plan with changes
    Given local build_dir differs from remote
    When Plan runs
    Then counts and bytes-to-send reflect rsync dry-run stats

  Scenario (happy-path): Already up to date
    Given local build_dir matches remote
    When Plan runs
    Then transferred counts are zero and unchanged equals local file count

  Scenario (edge): Dotfiles in the build tree
    Given a build_dir containing .git/, .env, .mason, nested dotfiles, and /.well-known/security.txt
    When Plan runs with --delete against a remote that already has a .git/
    Then only regular content and /.well-known/ are planned, and the remote .git/ is not removed

  Scenario (negative): Missing deploy config
    Given a site without a build folder or path
    When Plan runs
    Then it returns a validation error before rsync
